=== VERDICT ===
  fault class : bad_deploy
  fix class   : rollback
  confidence  : low
  evidence    : tr_17bac6ca26ef, tr_caf8e0180b8c, tr_90773266a7a2, tr_26dc62b881ac, tr_c0be4905172a
  root cause  : Checkout order placement fails at a single hop: checkoutservice's client call to shippingservice GetQuote. In all ten sampled traces that client span is the only errored leaf, and frontend/PlaceOrder inherit ERROR from it, while cart, Redis, currency, catalog and feature-flag calls all succeed in milliseconds [tr_17bac6ca26ef]. GetQuote fast-fails in ~2ms with no server-side span from shippingservice anywhere in 163 spans, the signature of rejection at connection/dispatch rather than a slow handler [tr_17bac6ca26ef]. checkoutservice is otherwise healthy: it keeps accepting orders, burns negligible self time, and has no recorded change in the 24h around onset [tr_90773266a7a2, tr_26dc62b881ac]. Failures are partial and stepwise — ~0.09% baseline to ~14.4% mean, peak ~31%, change points at 09:20:30 and 09:45:00 [tr_caf8e0180b8c] — consistent with a staged rollout of a shippingservice artifact that cannot serve GetQuote, with the refusing fraction growing. checkoutservice is the service that noticed, not the one that broke. No dispatch touched shippingservice, so this mechanism is inferred from the caller side.
  OPEN        : shippingservice was never dispatched against: its change history, logs, metrics and restart state are wholly unobserved, so the failing artifact is inferred, not seen.
  OPEN        : The gRPC status code and error text on the errored GetQuote span were not reported, leaving refusal vs. resolution failure vs. resource limit undistinguished.
  OPEN        : The 09:20:30 change point precedes the alert by ~26 minutes and nothing explains what happened then; no pre-09:47 traces were returned for comparison [tr_17bac6ca26ef].

