=== PROPOSAL ===
  action      : rollback_image (rollback)
  target      : shippingservice
  expect      : Redeploying shippingservice at the tag it ran before the 09:44:20 image update should stop the repeating JVM/agent bootstrap triple in Loki {service="shipping-service"} and restore Rust-style GetQuote/tracking-ID request lines; in Tempo, checkoutservice GetQuote client spans should gain a shippingservice server span and frontend root spans should stop carrying ERROR; in checkoutservice logs, each [PlaceOrder] line should again be followed by payment/email/message-write completions. shippingservice's own metrics return no samples in either window, so confirmation must come from logs and traces, not from its error ratio.
  within      : 300s
  risk        : If the recorded prior tag is not a good shippingservice build, or if no prior tag exists (never established by any result), the recreate leaves shipping down or replaces one broken artifact with another, extending the checkout outage. Any in-flight GetQuote calls are reset during the recreate.
  blast radius: shippingservice restarts; checkoutservice sees connection resets on GetQuote during the recreate, propagating to frontend and loadgenerator. quoteservice may see its inbound traffic resume. emailservice, accountingservice, paymentservice and frauddetectionservice see checkout traffic return if the fix works.
  if wrong    : Falsified if the bootstrap triple keeps recurring on its backoff cadence after the recreate, which would mean the kill reason (never retrieved: no exit code, OOM record, or probe event) is the real mechanism rather than the image; or if a Rust shippingservice serves requests yet checkoutservice PlaceOrder traces still error at the shipping hop.
  rests on    : tr_181e2307f6e2, tr_bae95b5ca8e5, tr_799375d506e3
