=== VERDICT ===
  fault class : bad_deploy
  fix class   : rollback
  confidence  : high
  evidence    : tr_181e2307f6e2, tr_bae95b5ca8e5, tr_799375d506e3, tr_bb422f1c2b87, tr_d1c72b473e8b, tr_b38c4f72e28b, tr_ffec66f99963
  root cause  : At 09:44:20, platform-automation updated the shippingservice image reference to an adservice-tagged artifact (ghcr.io/open-telemetry/demo:v1.2.1-adservice) [tr_181e2307f6e2]. The workload that came up is not shippingservice: its logs shift from Rust-style application gRPC handling (successful GetQuote responses and tracking IDs early in the window) to a bare, repeating JVM/OpenTelemetry-agent bootstrap sequence about ten times between 09:44:43 and 09:51:18, with backoff-shaped spacing and zero request-handling lines [tr_bae95b5ca8e5]. The pod therefore never reaches a serving state, so checkoutservice's client call to ShippingService/GetQuote fails fast with client-only spans, no shippingservice server span and negligible duration, aborting PlaceOrder before payment and propagating an ERROR to the frontend root [tr_799375d506e3]; checkoutservice logs show order placements arriving but no downstream completion lines from 09:48:56 onward [tr_bb422f1c2b87]. Checkoutservice is the caller that noticed, not the fault: it is alive, unchanged, and its own error ratio is indistinguishable from baseline [tr_b38c4f72e28b][tr_d1c72b473e8b]. The running artifact on shippingservice is the wrong one; reverting the image reference to the last good shippingservice build is the fix.
  OPEN        : No kill reason was retrieved for the shippingservice restarts — no exit code, OOM-kill record, or liveness-probe event; the crash-loop is inferred from repeated boot sequences with no terminal error line [tr_bae95b5ca8e5].
  OPEN        : shippingservice has no usable metrics at all: error ratio, request rate, p95 and saturation returned no samples in either incident or baseline window, so container memory/CPU at restart time is unmeasured [tr_ffec66f99963].
  OPEN        : The checkoutservice and currencyservice change queries covered 09:47 forward, not the hours before onset, so a pre-incident change to either service was never actually searched [tr_b38c4f72e28b][tr_51a418ba9460].
  OPEN        : Checkoutservice logs were truncated to the oldest 8 and newest 32 lines, so the exact onset of the stall between 08:47 and 09:48 and any error lines in that gap are unobserved [tr_bb422f1c2b87].
  OPEN        : Gap between the image update (09:44:20), the first restarts (09:44:43) and the checkoutservice alert (09:47:00) is unexplained in detail — likely rolling-update replica drain, but no deployment/replica evidence was gathered.
  OPEN        : quoteservice, emailservice, accountingservice and frauddetectionservice were never dispatched; their alerts are assumed downstream of shipping but not verified.
  OPEN        : Whether the last-known-good shippingservice image tag is identified and available for rollback is not established by any result.

